              "Request ordering"
            ],
            "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope",
            "notes": "Different hash outputs across clients cause block rejection at the CL, preventing finalization."
          },
          "test_procedure": "1. Identify all execution client implementations that implement compute_requests_hash (e.g., Geth, Nethermind, Besu, Erigon, Reth).\n2. Construct a canonical set of test inputs including: empty requests list, single request, multiple requests with varying sizes.\n3. Execute compute_requests_hash on each client implementation with identical input data.\n4. Compare the resulting SHA-256 hash outputs across all implementations to verify byte-for-byte identity.\n5. Verify the two-level SHA-256 construction: first hash each request individually, then feed all digests into the outer hash.\n6. Test with requests containing boundary values (empty bytes, null bytes, maximum length).\n7. Document any discrepancies and trace to root cause in the hashing implementation.",
