            "validation_layers": [
              "SHA-256 determinism",
              "Request ordering"
            ],
            "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope",
            "notes": "Different hash outputs across clients cause block rejection at the CL, preventing finalization."
          },
          "test_procedure": "1. Review the SHA-256 library/implementation used by each execution client.\n2. Verify that no floating-point operations, randomness, or platform-specific behavior affects hash computation.\n3. Test SHA-256 with NIST test vectors to confirm correctness.\n4. Verify byte ordering (endianness) is consistent across implementations.\n5. Check that hash state is properly initialized and finalized for each computation.\n6. Ensure no memory corruption or buffer issues can affect hash output.",
          "bug_class": "Cryptographic Implementation",
          "risk_category": "Tampering",
